          "@type": "Person",
          "name": "Peter Salib"
        }
      ],
      "datePublished": "2026",
      "description": "Letter to the editor responding to Yuval Noah Harari's objection to AI legal personhood. Argues that AI agents pursuing long-term goals can be disciplined through resource constraint: A-corps make agents visible and governable by giving the state the ability to see, tax, and seize their assets — legal personhood as a leash, not a master key.",
